If your bag isn't very full, you can #dip it in holy water or
whatever--in that case, just carry a spare sack with a holy water, ?
rc, whatever.

But if the bag is full (say, to the point where you're not _quite_
burdened when it's blessed), it gets INCREDIBLY HEAVY when cursed and
you can't carry it anywhere and can't do anything (including #dip it)
once it's cursed aside from drop it (and maybe a couple other moves).
Once it's dropped, you can't pick it up again (unless you empty it
out, risking the contents to random vanishing as usual with a cursed
bag).  So you either carry a /cancel, or have to leave the bag behind,
run grab a /cancel, and come back.

Or you learn the cancellation spell with a low enough failure rate to
make it acceptable (safer, since you can't accidentally put a spell in
your bag, but not always an option).



